            <ArticleTitle>Headaches and brain tumors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>423-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ncl.2013.11.006</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0733-8619(13)00120-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article overviews headache and brain tumors, particularly from the diagnostic point of view of patients presenting with headache as their major symptom. Common and uncommon brain tumors can produce headache and investigation is warranted if any red flags are present. An overview of particular tumors and their presentations are covered along with some investigative suggestions and pertinent treatment strategies for some patients.</AbstractText>
